WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:11.320
Hey, welcome back to 40 Days of Holiness. Today is day 37.

2
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.740
We're talking about emotions. Now, emotions, feelings, are

3
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.240
great and horrible. They're part of what makes us human,

4
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.980
right? And we can either figure out how to fight them or how to

5
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.030
recruit them to help in the project of holiness of heart and

6
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.200
holiness of life that God is calling you to.

7
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:32.400
So please, don't fight them. All right? Don't deny them.

8
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.420
At one point in my life, I made the mistake of thinking that I needed to be

9
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.200
this emotionless Christian, melancholy, and it was

10
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:40.720
terrible.

11
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.440
And I didn't please God. I'm sure I didn't please God as much as I should have

12
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:49.400
during that season, because God is pleased when we are emotionally happy

13
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.200
in Him. But sometimes people do make a mistake that makes their feelings their

14
00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.280
enemy of holiness instead of their friend.

15
00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.360
So I want to talk to you about that today.

16
00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.830
Frequently, a mistake that a lot of people make is

17
00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.030
connecting holiness so closely to their

18
00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.720
emotions that they feel as though their holiness

19
00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:11.020
rises and falls based on how they're feeling.

20
00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.770
How holy they're feeling, how excited they're feeling, how confident they're

21
00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.500
feeling, how saved they're feeling.

22
00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.820
People often do the same thing with marriage.

23
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.860
We think that love is a feeling, an emotion, and

24
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.760
we start dating, and we feel warm fuzzies, and we assume that's what love is.

25
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.670
But then we wake up next to that same person six years later,

26
00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:36.390
and they have bad breath, and their hair is a mess, and

27
00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.340
we have a headache, and we're not feeling good, and we're feeling grumpy that day,

28
00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:39.980
and we think,

29
00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:41.920
"Where did the love go?"

30
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.300
Well, love isn't a feeling. It might cause feelings, and those feelings

31
00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.980
may come, and they may go, but love itself is not a feeling.

32
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.900
It is a commitment, an action, a commitment to act in the

33
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.440
best interest of the other person.

34
00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.740
And you need to sustain your relationship with your spouse by

35
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.740
commitment, not feelings. And do two things to your emotions.

36
00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.740
Cultivate them and enjoy them.

37
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.400
Your feelings did not create your marriage, and they cannot

38
00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.910
destroy your marriage. Your feelings do not create your

39
00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.060
holiness, and they cannot destroy your holiness.

40
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.600
You are not saved, you are not made holy by feeling good about God

41
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.690
or yourself. Instead, you should reaffirm your

42
00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:30.580
commitment to the Lord when your emotions are down, and then cultivate the

43
00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.580
environment, the mindset, where the right emotions

44
00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.570
are possible. And this makes your emotions your

45
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.470
friend, the friend of your holiness, instead of the enemy of it.

46
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.890
Instead of fighting against me doing right and doing the will of God

47
00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.049
and living like Jesus and having His mind and His heart.

48
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:51.500
Instead of

49
00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.440
being the enemy of that, instead it becomes a support.

50
00:02:55.489 --> 00:02:59.480
It becomes a tailwind that pushes me further

51
00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.210
in my pursuit of God because I am glad in Him,

52
00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.000
and I'm joyful in Him.

53
00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.810
Now, tomorrow, we're going to talk about exactly

54
00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.800
how. I'm going to talk about some of the techniques, some of the ways to

55
00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:16.230
cultivate those emotions. But I just want to tell you for

56
00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.859
today, they can be your friend or your enemy. Don't deny them.

57
00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.600
Don't squash them. Don't consider them your enemy.

58
00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:27.700
Instead, find ways to recruit them so that they are your friend.

59
00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:32.160
Just find ways to cultivate the right emotions and make them possible,

60
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.670
and then enjoy them, and let them drive you further down the

61
00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.440
road on the project, and the following of holiness.

62
00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.000
We'll talk to you tomorrow.
